WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.234
A potentially historic

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.036
winter storm is pounding

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.005
parts of the Great Lakes region

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:08.008
to people in New York's Erie County died

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.876
after suffering cardiac events

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.444
related to clearing snow.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.545
Officials warn

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.347
that the storm could be life

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.416
threatening and have called on residents

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.451
to be prepared

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.455
Right now, we do have a travel ban

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.991
in South Buffalo.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.394
We have a travel advisory throughout

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.496
the rest of Buffalo.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.630
And we're asking people

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.399
if you don't need to go out.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.567
If travel is not necessary.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.570
Please stay at home so snow

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.873
plows can do their job.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.309
While the winter storm has canceled

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:46.413
flights, halted traffic on major roadways

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.048
and knocked out power

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.949
as temperatures plunge.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.552
Polo Sandoval has the story from Buffalo,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.453
New York.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:59.125
Yeah, we got some snow.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.594
Heavy snowfall, thunder, lightning.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.996
A potential historic

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.631
snowstorm is pummeling

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:05.432
areas surrounding

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.232
the Great Lakes

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.801
with western New York State

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:10.303
in the bull's eye. It's a little deep

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.441
Oh, my God.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.875
The storm already dumped around

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.409
four feet of

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.978
snow south of Buffalo, prompting the NFL

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.313
to move the Buffalo Bills.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.047
A Sunday game

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.016
to Detroit Highmark Stadium,

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.984
their usual home in Orchard Park,

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.153
left completely covered in white.

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:28.855
And the storm is expected to hit

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.457
the city hard on Friday night.

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.224
The National Weather

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.826
Service and New York officials

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.194
warning that the snowfall

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.228
will produce life

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.230
threatening conditions into the weekend

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.465
can turn very quickly.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.500
This is a very unpredictable storm.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.835
Even with the warnings

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.036
some people in Buffalo

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.370
don't seem too worried.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.107
We live in Buffalo. It's expected.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.675
That's all I could say.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:50.176
We've been through this before.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.444
It's not to me, it's no big deal.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.947
But my family wants everything done.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.081
Officials reminding people

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.749
to stay inside and off

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.550
the roads saying

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.885
there is a travel ban

00:01:58.885 --> 00:01:59.819
in South Buffalo

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:00.854
with many flights

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:03.089
in and out of the region canceled.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.924
Please stay indoors.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:05.525
Do not go out

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.794
unless it is an absolute emergency.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.496
National Weather Service forecasters

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:10.029
explained

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:10.630
lake effect

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.966
snow is fueling this extraordinary storm

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.368
that occurs when cold air blows over

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.636
warmer lake water

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.071
picking up more moisture

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.539
and leading to higher snow

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:21.007
amounts down stream

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:21.841
Climate experts

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.575
warn water

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.710
temperatures in the Great Lakes

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.812
grow increasingly warmer each year,

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.213
shortening the length of time

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.315
ice covers the surface during the winter.

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.750
I just want to remind everybody

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.085
that there is a lake effect

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.486
warning still in effect.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.088
So this thing is still moving.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.023
So we need to still take this series.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.459
Polo Sandoval, CNN, Buffalo, New York.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:44.130
CNN meteorologist Derek Van Dam

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:44.964
joins us now

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:45.832
live from the CNN

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.533
Weather Center

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.668
with more on all this Derek.

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:51.037
Leyla, these snow totals

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:51.871
I'm about to show

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.940
you are just mind boggling.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.276
But you've got to see this

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.411
almost a elevated view time

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.079
lapse of a snow squall.

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.681
This is the lake effect snow band

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.450
moving over downtown Buffalo earlier

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.052
on Friday.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:06.452
And you can

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.521
see the extreme whiteout conditions

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.323
that just basically inundate

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.891
and take over the city.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.226
This is a very narrow

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.794
band of heavy snowfall.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:15.695
We're talking

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:18.398
three upwards of five inches per hour

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:19.732
within that snow band,

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.135
but it's only a ten mile wide snow band.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.537
So dependent on where it's located.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:25.505
That's the location

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:26.339
that's getting the heaviest

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.441
snowfall at that particular time.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.710
Here's the snowfall totals as promised.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:31.978
That is an impressive,

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.913
incredible amount of snow.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.216
We're talking about nearing record

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.483
breaking territory

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.552
for the state of New York.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.588
That has to be officially closed

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.523
from the National Weather Service

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.325
and analyzed by some of the

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:47.794
the the measuring apparatuses

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.329
that are ongoing here, really

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.730
for all these various locations.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.798
But nonetheless,

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:52.498
that is just

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.300
a significant amount of snow.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.169
And it is significantly dangerous,

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:58.071
especially for households and businesses.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.405
There, just because of the sheer

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.140
weight of the snow.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.942
We've done the math for you.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.177
You can double check my math

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:04.744
if you'd like.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:05.845
You can follow me on Twitter

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.513
and correct me if I'm wrong on this one.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:08.681
But if we're looking at an average

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:09.949
square footage

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.418
of a house, 2000 square feet or so,

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:13.720
you multiply that

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.822
by four feet of snow on average,

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.690
depending on where we're talking about in

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.958
and around Buffalo.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:22.262
That equates to nearly £50,000

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.063
on top of your roof.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:26.232
That is like having ten

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:28.801
SUVs piled up on top of your building.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:29.469
That,

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.371
of course, could lead to some collapse

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.805
or failed roofs.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.641
And that is obviously dangerous,

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:35.174
not to mention

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.542
what's happening on the roadways.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.144
We have still over

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.646
6 million Americans

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.247
under these winter weather alerts,

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.515
including Michigan.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.250
But I'm really focusing our attention

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.718
downwind of Lake Erie

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:46.653
and Lake Ontario

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:47.787
because this is the area

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:48.821
that has been battered

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.624
for a good part of the past 48 hours.

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:53.026
And now that heavy snow

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:56.062
band moving directly over the downtown

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.096
area of Buffalo

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.531
so they're getting hit very hard

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.232
right now.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.366
This is a three hour loop,

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:01.968
but I want to go back 24 hours

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.403
because I want you to see

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:04.237
almost that

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:05.371
firehose of

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.639
snow that continues

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.407
to oscillate

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.975
north and south, depending

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.777
on the exact direction of the wind.

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:11.678
That's what I was talking about,

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.946
that narrow, heavy band of snowfall.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.449
It is so imperative and so critical

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.850
where that wind direction is,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.619
because that determines

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.521
who sees the whiteout conditions,

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:23.556
who sees the heaviest amounts of snow.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.458
So the question on everyone's minds,

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.293
how much more snow is still to come?

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:27.493
Well,

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.728
we have the potential for over

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:29.729
two feet of additional

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.331
snow through Sunday evening

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:33.166
across the Watertown region

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:35.535
into the northern Syracuse suburbs

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:36.302
and Buffalo

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:36.903
another foot

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:37.403
to a foot

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.105
and a half of additional snowfall

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:40.139
for you.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:42.241
These snowfall totals are tremendous

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:43.743
and they could be going down in the

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:44.944
record books. Time will tell.

